 innovations and  this is where our first two groups of  scitech recipients take center stage in  2002 the film The Chronicles of Narnia  The Lion the Witch and the Wardrobe  posted a help-wanted ad hundreds of  digital character rigs needed for  immediate work apply within to visual  effects Studios jumped at the chance to  take this challenge head-on so let's  learn a little about our first award of  the evening block party  [Applause]  The Chronicles of Narnia had massive  numbers of digital characters and each  would need a unique rig one of the  systems that arose from that need is  block party from Industrial Light and  Magic there were multiple versions of  character rigs going around I 11 the  thought was you know what if we can take  those complex units like an arm or a  spine and just make it this packaged  thing that can plug into the block next  to it and then create a character rig  that way the secret to block parties  automated and fast rig building is in  the title  it's literally like building with blocks  each block is a little piece of a rig  with a purpose like an arm or shoulder  so blocks are essentially mini rigs and  those little rigs piece themselves  together with lots of other different  blocks creating motion for the character  multiple blocks can be connected to  create a character and the blocks are  swappable so even after a full rig is  assembled if the artist wants a  different spine they can simply replace  it with another spine block moreover  once a complete rig is constructed it  can quickly repurpose for a different  character simply by fitting the original  rig to the new character our main goal  with my party really was to help make  the job of the rigger much simpler so  that they don't have to think about  those technical complexities every  second of every day while they're doing  their rigging block parties rigs can be  stored away for future use and since its  inception more than twenty four thousand  unique rigs have been created for almost  100 feature films many of which have  been nominated or received the Academy  Award for visual effects including  Pirates of the Caribbean Dead Man's  Chest Bloc Party has contributed to at  least one Oscar nominated film every  year since its birth as well as the  recent blockbusters Kong Skull Island  star wars the last Jedi and Thor  Ragnarok it's really really cool to be  able to support these artists who are  extreme perfectionist and  they do and make it possible to bring  bigger and better and more innovative  characters to the screen  tonight the Academy presents a technical  achievement award to Jason Smith Jeff  white Rachel Marie Rose and Michael  Justin lead Utah for their work  for their work on ILM block party come  on up to the stage  [Applause]  [Music]  so as many can attest the developing  developing technology for our industry  is often driven by pure passion for us  Bloc Party really epitomizes that  passion so thank you to the Academy for  honoring us and this technology that we  really love I'd also like to thank my  parents Carol and Dan for their endless  support over the years and to my husband  Justin and to my beautiful children  Clara and Damon thank you for standing  by my side through this journey and  finally to any young woman who may be  watching this and dreaming about her  future career I am proof that you can  [Music]  thank you cheers to those who strive for  creative solutions to complex problems  for example my epic wife Michal is nine  months pregnant our first child is due  tomorrow  but she said you got to go accept your  award well you better get on that last  plane to San Francisco tonight before I  have this baby we call your you're  insane I love you and thank you for all  the support  I'm also immensely grateful for my  parents cherylin are through ten who are  here tonight  thank you for your endless encouragement  to live a life filled with passion from  the career inspiring t1000 in Terminator  2 to Jon double Steen's talent amazing  talent visible in every bone in block  party we salute ILM s world-class  creature artists we'd also like to just  say a quick thank you to carry Phillips  in ILM for being the kind

